{
  "summary": "Adds an optional `control_block_warnings` field to `decodepsbt` to report why any Taproot input leaf script control block fails structural verification against BIP 341. It refactors four existing candidate checks from `InferTaprootTree()` into a shared `CheckTapLeafCandidate()` helper in `script/interpreter`. Unit test coverage is added for `InferTaprootTree()` failure modes along with RPC functional tests for invalid leaf records.",
  "problem": "When inspecting PSBTs with `decodepsbt`, `PSBT_IN_TAP_LEAF_SCRIPT` records are displayed verbatim even if their control blocks are invalid or cannot belong to the input's Taproot tree. While `InferTaprootTree()` performs these checks during signing, it silently drops invalid leaves without diagnostic feedback, making malformed or corrupted PSBTs hard to troubleshoot.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: '`InferTaprootTree()` already checks this, but silently skips whatever fails... a PSBT with an unusable leaf shows no sign of it.'",
    "PR description cites merged PR #25513 as precedent for adding similar Taproot verification diagnostics to PSBT outputs."
  ],
